<title>USA: Continued warm temps for Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</title>
<headline>Continued warm temps for Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The warm, subtropical ridge of high pressure currently dominating Brazil's coffee belt is expected to persist for the next seven days, Weather Services Corp said in an update Tuesday.</p>
<p>WSC expects mostly fair skies and near to above normal temperatures throughout the region. The lowest temperatures through Thursday morning will range from the middle 50's to the low 60's F (middle teens C).</p>
<p>Fair skies were observed in the coffee belt this morning. Low temperatures ranged from 54-61 F (12-16 C).</p>
<p>Scattered showers and thunderstorms may develop in the area for Wednesday and Thursday. Partly to variably cloudy skies are expected for Friday and Saturday. Temperatures should remain near to above normal with no damaging cold, according to WSC.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
